# Parsed by Workers static assets (never served as an asset itself, and never
# applied to Worker responses — /playlist and /segment set their own CORS).
#
# /cf.txt doubles as a cross-origin reachability beacon: the web client fetches
# it to tell "the relay is reachable from this browser" from "this browser is
# being challenged or blocked at the relay's edge". It is a static asset, so the
# probe costs no Worker request. Reading it cross-origin needs CORS, and the ASN
# (set by the Response Header Transform Rule — see README.md) needs exposing.
/cf.txt
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Access-Control-Expose-Headers: x-client-asn
